BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Inside Mass Tort Litigation: A Lunch Talk with Lead
 ing Plaintiffs’ Lawyers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T124500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T134500
DTSTAMP:20260825T135102Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003122-1790253900-1790257500@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-09-24T12:45:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Some of the nation’s most consequential litigation — over 
 the opioid crisis\, the Roundup herbicide\, and children’s safety on the
  Roblox platform — is being led by a small group of plaintiffs’ lawyer
 s. In this lunchtime talk\, some of these leading lawyers will discuss how
  cases of this scale are built and litigated\, what the day-to-day work of
  representing plaintiffs in mass torts and multidistrict litigation actua
 lly involves\, and what career paths in plaintiffs’-side litigation look
  like. Moder\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/ins
 ide-mass-tort-litigation-a-lunch-talk-with-leading-plaintiffs-lawyers/\nLa
 st synced: 2026-08-25 06:51 PDT
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 290\, 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stanford\, CA\, 94305-8
 610\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/inside-mass-tort-litigation-a-lunch-tal
 k-with-leading-plaintiffs-lawyers/
END:VEVENT
