BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Inside AI-Native: A Lunch Talk Exploring New Practi
 ce Models
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T124500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T140000
DTSTAMP:20260825T135102Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003230-1791204300-1791208800@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-10-05T12:45:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:AI-native law firms are dominating industry headlines. This mo
 del raises interesting questions about lawyer training and development\, i
 nnovation and R&D\, risk and compliance\, nonlawyer investment\, and regul
 atory frameworks\, among others. In this lunchtime talk\, lawyers at the f
 rontline of AI-native legal services innovation will consider how the AI-n
 ative model is transforming law practice. Open to the Stanford community\;
  no legal background required. Lunch provided.\n\nhttps://law.stanford.edu
 /ev\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/inside-ai-na
 tive-a-lunch-talk-exploring-new-practice-models/\nLast synced: 2026-08-25 
 06:51 PDT
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 290\, 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stanford\, CA\, 94305-8
 610\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/inside-ai-native-a-lunch-talk-exploring
 -new-practice-models/
END:VEVENT
