DTSTAMP:20260825T135102Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003127-1792500300-1792504800@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-10-20T12:45:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:American Caesarism examines whether the United States faces ri
 sks similar to those that transformed the Roman Republic into an autocracy
  under Julius Caesar—namely\, the concentration of power in a single cha
 rismatic leader who claims to embody the popular will while circumventing 
 traditional institutional constraints. During Donald Trump’s presidency
 \, scholars and commentators invoked this framework to analyze his norm-br
 eaking behavior: his attacks on judicial independence\, attempts to person
 al\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/american-caes
 arism-confronting-an-executive-unbound/\nLast synced: 2026-08-25 06:51 PDT
